## SQ-HTD-01 | rotten foods are hazard with 20% Poison II 5 s; three are no longer saltable
@group A
@commands `cdevtest food` each of the six; `cdevtest tag item salt:can_be_salted`; `cdevtest tag item creativedelight:food_type/hazard`
@pass Rotten Ham, Cooked Rotten Ham, Rotten Pie, Green Pie, Fried Turtle Egg and Suspicious Bacon and Eggs each list `minecraft:poison` amplifier 1, 100 ticks, chance 0.2, hunger and saturation as before (2/0.1, 4/0.3, 4/0.3, 5/0.4, 5/0.4, 8/1.0); all six in the hazard type tag; the salt tag has no rottenpie, greenpie or suspiciousbaconandaggs, still has cookedrottenham
@fails `hostile_items.js` modification not applied (MCreator item builds its FoodProperties elsewhere); `food_types.js` hostiledelight part stale in the jar
> cdevtest food hostiledelight:rottenham
> cdevtest food hostiledelight:cookedrottenham
> cdevtest food hostiledelight:rottenpie
> cdevtest food hostiledelight:greenpie
> cdevtest food hostiledelight:friedturtleegg
> cdevtest food hostiledelight:suspiciousbaconandaggs
> cdevtest tag item salt:can_be_salted
> cdevtest tag item creativedelight:food_type/hazard
waitlog verb=tag kind=item tag=creativedelight:food_type/hazard n= 30
expect verb=food item=hostiledelight:rottenpie\S* food=true .*effects=\S*minecraft:poison
expect verb=food item=hostiledelight:suspiciousbaconandaggs\S* food=true .*effects=\S*minecraft:poison
reject verb=tag kind=item tag=salt:can_be_salted n=\d+ ids=.*hostiledelight:(rottenpie|greenpie|suspiciousbaconandaggs)\b
